# GITHUB_OWNER / GITHUB_REPO identify the target APP's repo (not this repo)
# -- get_codebase_context_from_github() (agent/github_context.py) fetches
# its entire current source tree live via the GitHub API on every alarm, and
# open_or_update_issue() (agent/github_issue.py) opens/comments on an issue
# there with the diagnosis. For this project's demo app:
# GITHUB_OWNER=Tehreem404, GITHUB_REPO=bad_app_demo. GITHUB_REF is optional
# (defaults to the repo's default branch). GITHUB_TOKEN is optional for the
# read-only codebase fetch on public repos (60/hr unauthenticated vs 5000/hr
# with a token) but REQUIRED, with write access to that repo, for the
# GitHub issue step -- issue creation/comments are never possible
# unauthenticated regardless of repo visibility.
GITHUB_OWNER=
GITHUB_REPO=
GITHUB_REF=
GITHUB_TOKEN=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional -- empty = skip log evidence entirely (the app doesn't ship logs
# yet). Set this once log shipping exists.
LOG_GROUP=
# ARN of the existing alarm's SNS topic to subscribe the Lambda to, e.g.
# arn:aws:sns:us-east-1:<account-id>:culprit-alerts (deploy only, not used
# by run_manual.py).
ALARM_TOPIC_ARN=
